p.src:
A geodesic is a curve whose tangent is parallel transported along itself: $dt^n+\Gamma^n{}_{mr}t^r\,dx^m=0.$ Divide by $ds$ and use $dx^m/ds=t^m$: $\frac{dt^n}{ds}
=
-\Gamma^n{}_{mr}t^m t^r.$ Finally insert $t^n=dx^n/ds$: $\boxed{
\frac{d^2x^n}{ds^2}
+\Gamma^n{}_{mr}
\frac{dx^m}{ds}
\frac{dx^r}{ds}
=0.
}$

