p.src:
For a fixed worldline $r=R$, equation  gives $d\tau=R\,d\omega.$ Its four-velocity is $U^\mu
=
\frac{d(t,x)}{d\tau}
=
(\cosh\omega,\sinh\omega),$ and its four-acceleration is $A^\mu
=
\frac{dU^\mu}{d\tau}
=
\frac{1}{R}(\sinh\omega,\cosh\omega).$ The invariant magnitude is constant: $a=\sqrt{A^\mu A_\mu}=\frac{1}{R}
\qquad (c=1).$

